# signals' sources routes (core/modules/signals/README.md "API"), under the workspace. Two variables
# besides the usual ones go in http-client.private.env.json: `senderAccountId`, a sender account of the
# workspace (GET …/linkedin/accounts), and `sourceId`, the id the first request answers.

### POST /v1/workspaces/{workspaceId}/signals/sources: creates a source of a registered kind, enabled; 201 with the row
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/workspaces/{{workspaceId}}/signals/sources
Content-Type: application/json
Cookie: {{sessionCookie}}
Origin: {{appOrigin}}

{ "kind": "post_engagers", "config": { "postUrl": "https://www.linkedin.com/feed/update/urn:li:activity:7250000000000000000" }, "label": "Launch post", "senderAccountId": "{{senderAccountId}}" }

### GET /v1/workspaces/{workspaceId}/signals/sources: the workspace's sources, newest first, each with its next fire times (alpha-p8-040), runOpen, one of its runs running or waiting (alpha-p10-110), and openRun, that run's { id, status } or null (fix-run-wait)
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/workspaces/{{workspaceId}}/signals/sources
Accept: application/json
Cookie: {{sessionCookie}}

### PATCH /v1/workspaces/{workspaceId}/signals/sources/{id}: enables, disables or relabels a source
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/v1/workspaces/{{workspaceId}}/signals/sources/{{sourceId}}
Content-Type: application/json
Cookie: {{sessionCookie}}
Origin: {{appOrigin}}

{ "enabled": false, "label": "Launch post, paused" }

### GET /v1/workspaces/{workspaceId}/signals/sources/{id}/runs: the source's runs, newest first
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/workspaces/{{workspaceId}}/signals/sources/{{sourceId}}/runs
Accept: application/json
Cookie: {{sessionCookie}}

### DELETE /v1/workspaces/{workspaceId}/signals/sources/{id}: deletes the source and its runs; 204
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/v1/workspaces/{{workspaceId}}/signals/sources/{{sourceId}}
Cookie: {{sessionCookie}}
Origin: {{appOrigin}}
